# ── Real data: never in git ──────────────────────────────────────────
# Anchored to the repository root, every one of them, and that matters more than it looks.
# Unanchored, "backups/" also matched src/app/(app)/settings/backups/ — so the Backups screen,
# the Remits screen and the Reports screen were quietly never committed, and the site 404'd on
# them anywhere it was cloned. A rule meant to keep patient data out of git was deleting three
# features instead. These are directories that exist once, at the top of the project.
/data/
/uploads/
/private/
/contracts/
/reports/
/remits/
/backups/
*.835
*.837
*.edi
*.x12
*.xlsx
*.xls
*.csv
*.tsv
*.pdf
*.docx
*.doc
*.db
*.sqlite
*.sqlite3
*.dump
*.sql.gz
# Synthetic fixtures are the one exception; they live only here:
!fixtures/**

